== requests
  200 "GET a=1 \"\"\n"
  200 "PUT  \"hello\"\n"
  413 "too large\n"
  200 ""
  200 "one two three" (chunked)
  404 "not found\n"
http date: Sun, 09 Sep 2001 01:46:40 GMT, parsed back: true, garbage: true
host header carries the port: true
== keep-alive
  same connection: true
  new connection after close: true
== stall
  transient/link:  no progress for 0.5s
  200 "late\n"
== redial after the server dropped an idle connection
  200 "GET after=restart \"\"\n"
== nothing listening
  transient/link
== TLS listener
  openssl server, openssl client: 200
    without the CA: refused/other
  openssl server, ocaml-tls client: 200
    without the CA: refused/other
  ocaml-tls server, openssl client: 200
    without the CA: refused/other
  ocaml-tls server, ocaml-tls client: 200
    without the CA: refused/other
== TLS edge cases
  openssl: one 3000-byte record read 100 bytes at a time: 3000 bytes
  ocaml-tls: one 3000-byte record read 100 bytes at a time: 3000 bytes
  a client that never speaks TLS is dropped: end of stream
  a server that never speaks TLS fails the client: transient/link: TLS with localhost: no handshake within 0.3s
